playtimetracker.config.afkThresholdSeconds=AFK threshold (seconds)
playtimetracker.config.afkThresholdSeconds.tooltip=Inactivity after which the counter stops. The idle time already elapsed is taken back out of your played total and moved to AFK.
playtimetracker.config.minSessionSeconds=Shortest session kept (seconds)
playtimetracker.config.minSessionSeconds.tooltip=Sessions shorter than this are discarded entirely, so brief visits do not clutter your statistics. Set to 0 to keep every session.
playtimetracker.config.autosaveIntervalSeconds=Autosave interval (seconds)
playtimetracker.config.autosaveIntervalSeconds.tooltip=How often the data file is written. This also bounds how much of a running session a crash can cost you.
playtimetracker.config.retentionDays=Detailed history (days)
playtimetracker.config.retentionDays.tooltip=How long each session is kept in full detail. Older ones are merged into monthly summaries. No playtime is ever lost, only the detail.
playtimetracker.config.debugLogging=Log active/AFK transitions
playtimetracker.config.debugLogging.tooltip=Writes every switch between playing and AFK to the log. The mod is silent by default; turn this on to check that activity detection behaves as you expect.
